# SwiftFormat configuration.
#
# The tool choice and its enforcement are SPEC decisions:
# https://github.com/CalixtoTheBugHunter/talos/wiki/Engineering-Standards#toolchain
# CI runs `--lint`; developers autofix locally, which is what the pre-commit
# hook in `.githooks/pre-commit` does.

# Matches `swift-tools-version` in Package.swift. Without it SwiftFormat
# disables the rules that depend on knowing the language version, and says so.
--swiftversion 6.2

# The version the two options below were resolved against. An older binary does
# not know `--test-case-name-format`, so it would apply the default this file
# exists to override — and because the pre-commit hook autofixes rather than
# checking, that arrives as a rewritten file instead of an error. SwiftFormat
# exits non-zero here rather than formatting, which a CI pin cannot do: the pin
# governs the runner, and this governs whatever binary a contributor has.
--min-version 0.62.1

# SwiftLint's `trailing_comma` rejects a trailing comma in a collection literal
# and SwiftFormat's default (`always`) inserts one, so the two tools disagree
# and every file fails whichever runs second. The conflict is real and has to be
# resolved in one of the two files; it is resolved here because SwiftLint's rule
# is a default and this one is an option.
--trailing-commas never

# Keeps `@Test("...")` and `@Suite("...")` display names as written. The default
# (`raw-identifiers`) moves the string into a backticked raw identifier, and
# Swift Testing reports the same name at runtime — so it does not cost the
# property § Toolchain chose Swift Testing for. It is pinned because the rewrite
# is lossy at the edges: a backtick inside the display string is silently
# dropped, and a name containing an escape such as `\n` yields a raw identifier
# that does not compile. Both arrive as an autofix from the pre-commit hook
# rather than as an error.
--test-case-name-format preserve

# Build products, not sources — the same set `.swiftlint.yml` excludes.
--exclude .build,.swiftpm,DerivedData
